      "Calculate and include the correct unit in your answer"
    ],
    "title": "How to Solve Speed, Density & Pressure Problems",
    "content": "<p><strong>Speed</strong> = Distance ÷ Time. Use the triangle: cover the one you want to find.</p><p><strong>Density</strong> = Mass ÷ Volume. A denser object is heavier for its size.</p><p><strong>Pressure</strong> = Force ÷ Area. More force or less area means more pressure.</p><p>Always check <strong>units</strong> match. Convert hours ↔ minutes, cm³ ↔ m³, etc. before calculating.</p>",
    "example": "<p><strong>A car travels 150 km in 2.5 hours. Find its average speed.</strong></p><p><strong>Step 1:</strong> Speed = Distance ÷ Time</p><p><strong>Step 2:</strong> Speed = 150 ÷ 2.5 = 60 km/h</p>"
  },
